The '''Trapinch underground labyrinth''' is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive location underneath a grassland reserve on [[Izabe Island]] in the [[Hoenn]] [[region]]. It was featured in ''[[AG106|Beg, Burrow and Steal]]''.

The area is largely unknown as it is hidden deep underground. The confusing network of tunnels and its tendency to experience underground flooding make it particularly dangerous. Because of its shade and water supply, {{p|Trapinch}} like to nest in the labyrinth while they prepare to evolve into {{p|Vibrava}} during a seasonal mass [[Evolution]] event.

{{OBP|Hal|AG106}} discovered the secret oasis after falling down a Trapinch-dug hole as a child. He went on to dedicate his science career to studying Trapinch and locating the hidden labyrinth. In ''[[AG106|Beg, Burrow and Steal]]'', Hal found the labyrinth once again, this time accompanied by local {{tc|Pokémon Ranger}} [[Elisa]], {{Ash}}, and {{ashfr}}.

